<title>CANADA: Canadian foreign reserves fall in September.</title>
<headline>Canadian foreign reserves fall in September.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian foreign reserve holdings fell during September, the Finance Department said on Thursday.</p>
<p>   RESERVES			 Sept 96	Aug 96</p>
<p>   Total			   19.493 bln  19.603 bln</p>
<p>   U.S. dollars		  16.438 bln  16.505 bln</p>
<p>   Other foreign currencies     502 million     508 million</p>
<p>   Gold				 156 million     160 million</p>
<p>   Special drawing rights     1.162 bln   1.176 bln</p>
<p>   IMF reserves		   1.235 bln   1.249 bln</p>
<p>Note - Figures in U.S. dollars.  </p>
<p>Official government operations decreased reserves by US$65 million.</p>
<p>Details of the changes in the month:</p>
<p>    Gain on gold sales		    +3</p>
<p>    Earnings on investments	    +78</p>
<p>    Revaluation effects		  -46</p>
<p>    Foreign currency debt	     -101</p>
<p>    Other transactions		   +16</p>
<p>NOTE - in millions of U.S. dollars  </p>
<p>During September, Canada bills decreased by $157.7 million to a level of outstanding bills of $4.837 billion. Sales of Canada notes totalled $57 million, increasing the level of outstanding notes to $1.435 billion.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745</p>
